            "neonatal", "neonatologist + педиатр", "intermediate",
            "Cleft + hand abnormalities + IUGR + facial dysmorphism. Lifelong learning, behavioural challenges. Prevention through abstinence.",
            "## Spectrum\n\n### FAS (Fetal Alcohol Syndrome) — most severe\n- Distinct facial features:\n  - Smooth philtrum\n  - Thin vermilion (upper lip)\n  - Short palpebral fissures\n- **CNS dysfunction**\n- **Growth restriction** (height/weight < 10th percentile)\n- Cause: documented prenatal alcohol exposure\n\n### Partial FAS (pFAS)\n- 2 of 3 facial features\n- CNS dysfunction\n- Documented exposure\n\n### ARND (Alcohol-Related Neurodev Disorder)\n- CNS dysfunction\n- Documented exposure\n- НЕТ facial features OR growth restriction\n\n### ARBD (Alcohol-Related Birth Defects)\n- Specific congenital anomalies\n- Cardiac (VSD, ASD), skeletal, renal, ocular\n\n## Pathophysiology\n\nAlcohol crosses placenta freely. Effects depend on:\n- **Timing:** facial features (3-9 нед), CNS (any trimester)\n- **Quantity:** binge drinking worse than moderate continuous\n- **Genetic:** maternal + fetal metabolism (ADH1B, ALDH2)\n- **No safe threshold** documented\n\n## Newborn presentation\n\n- **IUGR / SGA** (often)\n- **Facial dysmorphism** (variable)\n- **Microcephaly** (CNS underdevelopment)\n- **Hypotonia, jitteriness**\n- **Tremulous, irritable**\n- **Poor feeding**\n- **Sleep dysregulation**\n- **Cardiac defects** (VSD, ASD common)\n- **Renal anomalies**\n\n## Workup\n\n- Detailed maternal history (alcohol, polysubstance)\n- Tox screen у mother + neonate (meconium / urine; meconium = chronic exposure)\n- Hair analysis (chronic exposure)\n- **NEPSY-II / Bayley III** longitudinal\n- Cardiac echo, renal US (anomalies)\n- Ophthalmology (microphthalmia, optic nerve hypoplasia)\n- Auditory screening\n- Genetic evaluation (rule out chromosomal that mimics)\n\n## Treatment / management\n\n### Acute newborn\n- **Withdrawal management** if needed (rare у newborn от alcohol — usually mild)\n- Supportive care\n- Skin-to-skin, breastfeeding если возможно\n- Establish feeding\n\n### Long-term\n- **Early intervention services** (PT, OT, speech)\n- **Special education** preschool / school\n- **Behavioural therapy**\n- **ADHD treatment** (very common)\n- **Speech / language therapy**\n- **Family support / counseling**\n- **CPS involvement** if maternal substance abuse continues\n\n### Cognitive / behavioural outcomes\n- **IQ:** average 60-80 (can range 30-120)\n- **Executive function deficits**\n- **Memory issues**\n- **ADHD** (60-90 %)\n- **Conduct disorder, depression**\n- **Impaired social skills**\n- **Sensory processing issues**\n\n## Prevention\n\n- **Universal pregnancy screening** alcohol use (T-ACE, TWEAK, AUDIT-C)\n- **Brief intervention + referral** при positive screen\n- **NO safe alcohol level** в pregnancy — abstinence advised\n- **Maternal MAT** при concurrent opioid use disorder\n- **Postnatal community supports**\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-prematurity-class (если SGA)\n- neo-newborn-screening\n- neo-discharge-criteria\n\n## Источники\n- AAP Section on Substance Use 2024\n- Hoyme HE et al. Pediatrics 2016;138:e20154256 — Updated criteria\n- CDC NCBDDD Guidelines 2024",
            ["Hoyme HE et al. Pediatrics 2016;138:e20154256", "AAP 2024", "CDC NCBDDD 2024"],
