            "1/700 livebirths. Multidisciplinary team approach. Specialized feeding (Haberman, Pigeon). Repair: lip 3-6 мес, palate 9-18 мес. Long-term speech / hearing.",
            "## Epidemiology\n\n- Cleft lip ± palate: 1/700 livebirths\n- Cleft palate isolated: 1/2000\n- Boys > girls (lip/palate)\n- Girls > boys (palate isolated)\n- Higher Asian, Native American populations\n\n## Etiology\n\n### Genetic\n- 25-30 % syndromic:\n  - Stickler syndrome (most common)\n  - Van der Woude (lip pits)\n  - 22q11.2 deletion (DiGeorge)\n  - Treacher Collins\n  - Pierre Robin sequence (small jaw → cleft palate)\n\n### Multifactorial (most common)\n- Genetic susceptibility + environmental triggers\n- Folate deficiency\n- Maternal smoking\n- Alcohol, antiepileptics (phenytoin, valproate), retinoids\n- Maternal diabetes\n\n## Classification\n\n### Cleft lip\n- **Unilateral** — most common\n- **Bilateral**\n- **Microform** (incomplete)\n\n### Cleft palate\n- **Hard palate** (anterior)\n- **Soft palate** (posterior)\n- **Submucous** (covered by mucosa — often missed)\n- **Complete** (lip + palate)\n\n## Initial assessment\n\n- **Genetic evaluation** (chromosome microarray, syndromic features)\n- **Cardiac echo** (associated CHD)\n- **Renal US**\n- **Hearing screen** (Eustachian tube dysfunction → middle ear effusion common)\n- **Otolaryngology consult** (airway, ear)\n- **Plastic surgery consult** (timing repair)\n- **Genetic counseling** (recurrence risk)\n\n## Feeding management\n\n### Challenges\n- Inability к create suction (cleft palate)\n- Nasal regurgitation\n- Choking, fatigue\n- Inadequate intake → failure to thrive\n\n### Specialized bottles\n- **Haberman feeder** (Special Needs Feeder) — squeeze-trigger flow\n- **Pigeon bottle** (cleft palate) — one-way valve\n- **Mead Johnson bottle** — soft squeeze\n- **Cup feeding** (for larger infants)\n- **NG tube** if PO not adequate\n\n### Lactation\n- Direct breastfeeding usually NOT possible (cleft palate)\n- Breast milk via bottle (specialized)\n- Pump + bottle-feed\n- Lactation consultant essential\n\n### Position\n- **Upright** или 45° angle\n- Frequent burping\n- Slow pace (avoid aspiration)\n\n## Pre-surgical orthopedics (large cleft)\n\n- **Naso-alveolar molding (NAM)** — preferred у severe bilateral CL/CP\n- Custom appliance reshapes alveolus + nostril\n- 6-12 weeks pre-surgery\n- Improves surgical outcomes\n\n## Surgical timing\n\n### Cleft lip repair\n- **3-6 мес** (Millard, Mohler, или Tennison-Randall techniques)\n- Adequate nutritional status (10-10-10 rule: 10 wks, 10 lb, Hb 10)\n\n### Cleft palate repair (palatoplasty)\n- **9-18 мес** (typical 12 мес)\n- Earlier (3-6 мес) controversial — better speech, less midface growth\n- Two-flap (von Langenbeck) или Furlow palatoplasty common\n\n### Subsequent surgeries\n- **Lip / nose revision** ~5 yr\n- **Velopharyngeal incompetence** repair if persistent (5-7 yr)\n- **Alveolar bone graft** (8-12 yr) — for tooth eruption\n- **Orthognathic surgery** (15-18 yr) если midface hypoplasia\n\n## Long-term issues\n\n### Speech / language\n- Articulation difficulties\n- Velopharyngeal insufficiency (hypernasal speech)\n- Speech therapy starting 2-3 yr возраста\n\n### Hearing / ENT\n- **Middle ear effusion** 90 % cleft palate (Eustachian tube dysfunction)\n- **Myringotomy + tubes** часто needed\n- **Hearing loss** intermittent\n- Annual ENT follow-up\n\n### Dental\n- Missing teeth, malocclusion\n- Orthodontics\n- Dental implants later\n\n### Psychological\n- Body image issues\n- Bullying support\n- Family counseling\n\n## Multidisciplinary cleft team\n\nIdeal cleft care:\n- Plastic / oral-maxillofacial surgery\n- Otolaryngology (ENT)\n- Pediatric dentistry / orthodontics\n- Speech-language pathology\n- Audiology\n- Genetics\n- Pediatrics / neonatology\n- Social work\n- Psychology\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-feeding-readiness\n- neo-discharge-criteria\n\n## Источники\n- ACPA (American Cleft Palate-Craniofacial Association) Standards 2024\n- Lewis CW et al. Pediatrics 2017;139:e20170628 — AAP Statement\n- Mossey PA et al. Lancet 2009;374:1773",
