            "Mother Rh-negative + father Rh-positive → maternal RhIG 300 мкг IM at 28 нед + post-delivery if fetus Rh-positive. Prevents alloimmunization для future pregnancies.",
            "## Background\n\n- ~15 % white population Rh-negative\n- Если Rh-negative mother + Rh-positive fetus + fetomaternal hemorrhage → maternal antibodies (anti-D) develop\n- **Future pregnancies** с Rh-positive fetus → severe HDFN (hemolytic disease of fetus + newborn)\n- **Prevention** через passive anti-D antibodies (RhIG) eliminates fetal Rh+ RBCs before maternal immune system responds\n\n## Indications для maternal RhIG\n\n### Antenatal\n- **28 нед routine** в всех Rh-negative pregnant women (если father unknown или Rh-positive)\n- **After amniocentesis, CVS, percutaneous umbilical blood sampling**\n- **External cephalic version** (ECV)\n- **Trauma** (any abdominal trauma в pregnancy)\n- **Threatened miscarriage / vaginal bleeding** > 12 нед gestation\n- **Ectopic pregnancy** (any gestation)\n- **Spontaneous/induced abortion**\n\n### Postnatal\n- **Within 72 ч delivery** if neonate Rh-positive\n- Verify через cord blood Rh typing\n\n## Dose\n\n- **Standard:** 300 мкг (1500 ЕД) IM\n- **Mini-dose:** 50 мкг для < 12 нед gestation events\n- **High dose** post-massive fetomaternal hemorrhage (Kleihauer-Betke ≥ 30 мл fetal blood):\n  - Calculate: ((K-B % × 50) / 30) × 300 мкг\n  - Round up к nearest 300 мкг increment\n\n## Newborn workup if mother Rh-negative\n\n- **Cord blood:** ABO, Rh, DAT (Coombs)\n- Rh-positive newborn → confirm RhIG given к mother postnatally\n- Direct Coombs (DAT) positive у newborn → ABO/Rh sensitization (mother previously sensitized)\n\n## Prevention failure\n\n### Reasons\n- Inadequate antenatal RhIG (missed dose, late dose)\n- Massive fetomaginal hemorrhage > 30 мл\n- Maternal RhIG dose inadequate\n- Trauma without recognition\n- Previous undocumented sensitization (other transfusions, ectopic, abortion)\n\n### If failure detected\n- Maternal antibodies (anti-D) detectable on indirect Coombs\n- Future pregnancies require:\n  - Serial maternal antibody titers\n  - MCA Doppler PSV для fetal anemia screening\n  - Intrauterine transfusion (IUT) если severe anemia\n  - Early delivery если hydrops imminent\n\n## Adverse effects RhIG\n\n- Pain at injection site (mild)\n- Anaphylaxis (rare < 1 / 100000)\n- Hemolysis (very rare с modern formulations)\n- Disease transmission risk minimal (heat-treated, screened donors)\n\n## Calculator Bordik\n- neo-bili-2022 (HDFN management)\n- neo-exchange-volume\n- neo-hdn-class\n\n## Источники\n- ACOG Practice Bulletin 192 (2018) — RhD alloimmunization\n- AAP Red Book 2024-2027\n- WHO Guidelines on Use Anti-D Immunoglobulin 2024",
